  "interpretation": {
    "summary": "Uncertainty-modulated opacity is the first downstream intervention in this study to be directionally better than both the fixed-opacity baseline and shuffled-confidence control in four of five exposed rooms.",
    "heterogeneity": "The median gain is modest and the descriptive interval crosses zero because ca1m-45261587 is slightly negative and ca1m-42897538 contributes a large positive effect.",
    "mechanism": "The strongest room improves metric correctness while reducing coverage modestly and substantially lowering MAE/p95, consistent with uncertainty-dependent visibility suppressing incorrect frontmost splats rather than simply increasing support.",
    "confirmatoryDecision": "Mechanistically promising enough to justify a separately frozen untouched U6b confirmatory study. U6a itself cannot establish efficacy."
